# House style

Full rules in AGENTS.md at the repository root. The two that are broken most often:

## No em dashes

Never use an em dash anywhere: code, comments, docs, UI strings, commit messages.
Use a comma, a full stop, a colon, brackets, or a plain hyphen. If none of those
fit, rewrite the sentence. Avoid the en dash too unless it is a numeric range.

The long lines in comment headers are box-drawing characters, not dashes. Leave
them alone.

## Nothing hardcoded that should be derived

If a value can be read, computed or configured, do that instead of typing it in.
A literal is a second source of truth and the two drift.

No hardcoded counts, prices, URLs, paths, model whitelists, magic numbers, or
sizes quoted in prose. Two values that must agree belong in one place both read;
if they cannot share a definition, add a test that fails when they disagree.
